# Plugins are community-owned — Forja does not know plugins

Index: [external plugins vs host](./forja-external-plugins-host.mdc) · [catalog hubs](./catalog-hub-host-generic.mdc) · [host tests](./forja-host-tests-no-pack-contracts.mdc)

## Model

| Tree | Role |
|------|------|
| `apps/forja/`, `packages/rust/` | **Host / foundation** — generic runtime, kit, player, engine contracts |
| [forja-packs](https://github.com/mGhassen/forja-packs) | **Community packs** — separate repo; not part of the host binary |

The root app ships **infrastructure to install, run, and render plugins**. It does **not** ship knowledge of which packs exist.

Treat every pack as **replaceable, renameable, and absent**. A user may install zero official hubs and only community packs. Local/dev: `FORJA_PACKS_ROOT` or sibling `forja-packs/` checkout.

---

## Forbidden in host (including `shared/engine`, `shared/foundation`, shell, settings)

| Do not | Why |
|--------|-----|
| Hardcode hub slot / tab inventories (`home`, `anime`, `asian_drama`, `arabic`, `live_sports`, `my_list`→`mylist`, …) | Pack folder names are community inventory |
| Map official slot → Features id tables in Dart | Packs declare `nav.tabId` / host uses opaque URL slot only |
| Branch host behavior on plugin ids (`kisskh`, `tmdb`, `anilist`, `forjahq-*`) | Pack ids are not host API |
| Seed nav / Features / PlatformDefaults with shipped hub lists | Empty host; packs register via `nav` on install |
| Assert shipped pack trees in host tests | See [host tests](./forja-host-tests-no-pack-contracts.mdc) |

```
❌ PluginRegistry.officialHubNavIdForSlot = { home, anime, asian_drama, … }
❌ switch (slot) { case 'live_sports': … }
❌ PlatformDefaults / seedBuiltIns listing hub tab ids
✅ hostNavId: authorTabId if set, else opaque forjaHqSlot(url), else p_<hash>
✅ Pack manifest nav.tabId when prefs need a stable id different from folder name
```

---

## Allowed in host (generic only)

- Parse **opaque** manifest fields, `nav`, `open.surface`, kit layout
- Path mechanics: `forjaHqSlot(url)` → last path segment (any string)
- Pack **kind** buckets from URL tree shape (`providers`, `hubs`, `live`, …) as install UI grouping — not a hub name allowlist
- Host **route surfaces** (`open.surface`) as kit destinations — not permission to list which packs exist

---

## Where pack knowledge lives

| May know scrapers / pack ids / hub folders | Must not |
|-------------------------------------------|----------|
| forja-packs only | `apps/forja/**`, `packages/rust/**` (except opaque passthrough) |

When adding a hub or provider: change the pack. Do not teach the host a new name.

---

## Foundation / design system

Do not “fix” product gaps by hardcoding pack lists into foundation or engine registries. That messes with foundation: shared code stays **generic kits**, not a ForjaHQ catalog index.
